{"id": "3eaaf28e-0a2e-4a64-931a-2e8d15637220", "role": "assistant", "block_type": "thinking", "content": [{"type": "text", "text": "This is a general troubleshooting question I can answer directly, not something requiring product lookup. The likely culprit is missing KMS permissions on the role—probably lacking kms:Decrypt or kms:GenerateDataKey, or the key policy itself doesn't grant access to that role, even though S3 access looks fine.

Other possibilities worth considering: bucket policy denies, VPC endpoint restrictions, cross-account issues, SCPs, permissions boundaries, session policies, using the wrong role entirely, S3 Access Points, or object ownership settings. The error message itself is a good clue—KMS-related denials typically mention kms:Decrypt explicitly, while a generic S3 AccessDenied points elsewhere. I should give a concise, practical fix with an example policy snippet.

